{"id":"vov-002","category":"Digital Wellness","subcategory":"Envy Management","content_type":"situation_based","title":"The Highlight Reel Pause","affirmation":null,"situation":"Feeling a sense of lack or inadequacy while viewing a peer's curated highlight reel online.","tone":"realistic","purpose":"To contextualize social media content and transform envy into information about personal values.","duration_minutes":5,"practice_steps":["Pause scrolling and notice the physical sensation of envy.","Remind yourself this is a curated snapshot, not a full reality.","Name the emotion without judgment and ask what you actually want for yourself."],"reflection_questions":["What specific element of this post triggers my envy?","Does this trigger a desire for the object, or a desire for the feeling it represents?"],"journaling_prompt":"If I stripped away the social prestige of this achievement, would I still actually want it for myself?","closing_message":"Envy is often a map pointing toward what we actually value.","tags":["envy","comparison","emotional-intelligence"]}
{"id":"vov-003","category":"Digital Wellness","subcategory":"Authentic Desire","content_type":"practice","title":"Marketing vs. Meaning","affirmation":null,"situation":null,"tone":"empowering","purpose":"To distinguish internal desires from external marketing influences.","duration_minutes":15,"practice_steps":["List three recent goals or purchases inspired by social media.","Identify the source of each desire and the perceived benefits promised by the influencer or image.","Compare these benefits against your top three personal core values.","Determine if the desire is about the thing itself or the validation it brings."],"reflection_questions":["Would I still want this if no one knew I had it?","How does this desire align with my actual daily lived experience?"],"journaling_prompt":"Describe a time you felt truly fulfilled by an activity that no one else saw or praised.","closing_message":"Your authentic desires are quiet but enduring.","tags":["authenticity","consumerism","values"]}

