{"id":"mc-001","category":"Mindful Communication","subcategory":"High-Stakes Dialogue Preparation","content_type":"practice","title":"Integrating Insight Meditation and CBT for Difficult Conversations","affirmation":null,"situation":"Preparing for a sensitive conversation with a partner or boss","tone":"grounding","purpose":"Reduce reactivity and improve listening presence by combining insight meditation with cognitive-behavioral strategies","duration_minutes":15,"practice_steps":["Sit quietly for two minutes focusing on the physical sensation of breath to anchor your nervous system.","Identify the specific emotion arising—such as anxiety or frustration—and label it without judgment.","Use a CBT thought record to identify one catastrophic prediction about the outcome and reframe it using evidence.","Plan three 'I' statements to communicate your needs without assigning blame.","Commit to a pause technique: take one full breath before responding to any challenging statement.","Set an intention to listen more than you speak."],"reflection_questions":["Did I listen to understand, or was I listening to respond?","At what point did I feel my reactivity increase, and how did I handle it?","How accurately did I reflect back what I heard?","What physical sensations arose during the talk?"],"journaling_prompt":"Describe one moment during the conversation where you felt triggered; how did you navigate that sensation in the moment?","closing_message":"Communication is a skill developed through practice. You showed up with intention, and that is enough for today.","tags":["mindfulness","cbt","communication","emotional-regulation"]}
