{"id":"res-001","category":"Mind-Body Resilience","subcategory":"Somatic Awareness","content_type":"practice","title":"Somatic Reset for Chronic Stress","affirmation":null,"situation":null,"tone":"grounding","purpose":"Validate physical fatigue and regulate the nervous system through gentle awareness rather than forced positivity.","duration_minutes":10,"practice_steps":["Sit or lie down comfortably and close your eyes.","Scan your body from head to toe, noticing areas of tension, heaviness, or numbness.","Breathe slowly into those areas without attempting to force the tension to disappear.","Acknowledge your exhaustion: 'My body is tired, and that is an honest response to my stress.'","Rest for two minutes without expecting productivity afterward."],"reflection_questions":["Where do you hold stress physically right now?","What does your body need most in this moment?","How does validating exhaustion change your relationship with it?"],"journaling_prompt":"Describe the physical sensations of your stress today and write a compassionate letter to that part of your body.","closing_message":"Rest is a biological necessity, not a reward. You are allowed to be tired; your body is simply processing your experience.","tags":["mindfulness","somatic","stress-relief","neuroscience","self-compassion"]}
