{"id":"focus-recovery-001","category":"Burnout Recovery","subcategory":"Sustainable Pacing","content_type":"practice","title":"Sustainable Focus Recovery Routine","affirmation":"Rest is part of my work, not a reward for finishing everything.","situation":"Feeling overwhelmed by lost time or pressure to hustle despite exhaustion.","tone":"realistic","purpose":"To reset the nervous system and redefine productivity through a neuroscience lens.","duration_minutes":20,"practice_steps":["Engage in 4-7-8 breathing to activate the parasympathetic nervous system.","Acknowledge feelings of guilt over lost time and identify physical signs of burnout.","Label 'lost time' as 'essential recovery time' for your brain.","Write down a list of non-negotiable rest activities for the day.","Choose one priority task that aligns with energy levels, not urgency.","Pause every 30 minutes to check in with stress levels."],"reflection_questions":["What does a successful day look like if it includes total rest?","Where am I forcing progress instead of allowing it?","Is my fear of falling behind based on facts or feelings?"],"journaling_prompt":"List three ways that resting today supports your long-term vision rather than hindering it.","closing_message":"You are allowed to move at a human pace. Consistency matters more than intensity.","tags":["burnout","mindfulness","entrepreneurship","focus","reframing"]}
