{"id": "career_toolkit_002", "category": "Decision Science", "subcategory": "Heuristics", "content_type": "practice", "title": "Satisficing Strategy", "affirmation": null, "situation": "Feeling paralyzed by too many options and the fear of missing the perfect one.", "tone": "grounding", "purpose": "Apply a decision science heuristic to reduce analysis paralysis and enable action.", "duration_minutes": 15, "practice_steps": ["Define your three non-negotiable criteria for a 'good enough' career path.", "Evaluate options sequentially against these minimum requirements.", "Select the first option that meets all criteria rather than searching for the absolute best.", "Commit to reviewing the choice later once you have real-world data."], "reflection_questions": ["What criteria are truly essential versus ideal?", "What is the cost of waiting for a perfect option?", "How does focusing on a satisfactory choice change my anxiety level?"], "journaling_prompt": "Describe the difference between a 'perfect' choice and a 'functional' choice in your current context.", "closing_message": "Accepting a 'good enough' choice allows you to gain real-world data that no amount of thinking can provide.", "tags": ["satisficing", "decision-making", "action"]}
{"id": "career_toolkit_003", "category": "Self-Reflection", "subcategory": "Emotional Analysis", "content_type": "situation_based", "title": "Fear Versus Intuition Analysis", "affirmation": null, "situation": "Unable to tell if a feeling of dread is a warning sign (intuition) or a fear of failure (anxiety).", "tone": "gentle", "purpose": "Distinguish between protective intuition and paralyzing fear.", "duration_minutes": 20, "practice_steps": ["Identify the specific physical feeling in your body.", "Ask yourself if this feeling indicates the path is wrong, or if you are afraid of failing at it.", "Write down the objective evidence for both possibilities."], "reflection_questions": ["Is this fear based on a specific known risk or a general fear of the unknown?", "Would I still feel this way if the outcome were guaranteed to be acceptable?"], "journaling_prompt": "List your fears objectively. Next to each, write evidence for and against it. Note any intuitive nudges separately, and contrast a time you followed intuition with a time fear decided.", "closing_message": "Understanding the source of your hesitation helps you make a choice based on values rather than avoidance.", "tags": ["intuition", "fear", "self-awareness"]}

