{"id": "grief-support-ya-01", "category": "Emotional Support", "subcategory": "Bereavement", "content_type": "situation_based", "title": "Supporting a Grieving Friend with Authenticity", "affirmation": "Your presence matters more than perfect words when walking alongside someone in grief.", "situation": "A close friend is navigating the loss of a loved one and you want to offer support without minimizing their pain.", "tone": "gentle", "purpose": "To provide empathetic, non-intrusive support that honors the grieving process.", "duration_minutes": 15, "practice_steps": ["Reach out simply without expecting an immediate reply", "Listen deeply without offering solutions or silver linings", "Acknowledge the loss directly using the deceased's name", "Validate their feelings with phrases like 'It makes sense that you feel this way'", "Allow silence to exist without rushing to fill it", "Offer concrete help like meals or errands", "Check in consistently after the initial flurry of support fades", "Respect their unique timeline and need for space"], "reflection_questions": ["What fears arise when thinking about saying the wrong thing?", "How can I remain present without trying to fix their pain?", "What boundaries do I need to maintain my own stability?"], "journaling_prompt": "Write about a time you felt truly heard during a difficult moment and how that presence impacted you.", "closing_message": "Grief has no timeline. Your steady, quiet support is a gift in itself.", "tags": ["grief", "friendship", "communication", "empathy", "mental-health"]}
