{"id":"ldr_003","category":"Relationship Maintenance","subcategory":"Communication","content_type":"practice","title":"The 'I' Statement Framework","affirmation":"I trust my ability to handle difficult emotions while waiting for connection.","situation":"Feeling neglected and wanting to bring it up without starting an argument.","tone":"empowering","purpose":"To articulate needs clearly and non-accusatorily.","duration_minutes":15,"practice_steps":["Identify the specific emotion you are feeling (e.g., lonely, anxious).","Describe the behavior without judgment (e.g., 'We haven't spoken in two days').","Express the need clearly (e.g., 'I would feel more connected if we had a scheduled call')."],"reflection_questions":["Did focusing on my feelings rather than their actions change the tone of my thoughts?","How does it feel to be clear about my needs?"],"journaling_prompt":"Write a draft of your request using the formula: 'I feel [emotion] when [behavior], and I would appreciate [specific action].","closing_message":"Clear communication is a tool for growth, not a sign of weakness.","tags":["communication","boundaries","ldr"]}

{"id": "perf_reframe_01", "category": "Personal Development", "subcategory": "Perfectionism", "content_type": "situation_based", "title": "Reframing Mistakes and Deliverables", "affirmation": "Mistakes are learning opportunities, not definitions of my worth or potential.", "situation": "Internship task error. Thought: 'If this deliverable isn't flawless, I've completely failed and proved I don't belong here.'", "tone": "realistic", "purpose": "Shift from binary success/failure thinking to a growth mindset and reduce anxiety around errors.", "duration_minutes": 5, "practice_steps": ["Identify the specific error without judging yourself.", "Challenge the thought with evidence of your previous good work.", "Draft a plan to correct the mistake and learn from it."], "reflection_questions": ["What would I tell a friend who made this mistake?", "What is the actual cost of a small mistake compared to the value of the lesson?"], "journaling_prompt": "Write about a time a mistake led to a valuable learning opportunity.", "closing_message": "You are here to learn, not to know everything already. Your value is not defined by a single error.", "tags": ["internship", "perfectionism", "growth mindset"]}
