{"id":"indigenous-leader-burnout-001","category":"Burnout Recovery","subcategory":"Rest","content_type":"affirmation","title":"Permission to Rest","affirmation":"Resting is an act of resilience that allows me to serve my community and myself with a full heart.","situation":null,"tone":"grounding","purpose":"Reduce guilt associated with downtime and validate the duality of modern professional and traditional roles.","duration_minutes":null,"practice_steps":[],"reflection_questions":[],"journaling_prompt":"In what ways does my cultural identity make me a more effective leader, and what does a truly restful hour look like for me today?","closing_message":"Your value is not defined by your productivity. You do not have to choose between your success and your soul.","tags":["rest","indigenous-leadership","recovery","identity"]}
{"id":"indigenous-leader-burnout-002","category":"Burnout Recovery","subcategory":"Mindfulness","content_type":"practice","title":"Ancestral Grounding Breath","affirmation":null,"situation":null,"tone":"grounding","purpose":"Reconnect with cultural identity to center the self during high-stress corporate days.","duration_minutes":5,"practice_steps":["Sit comfortably with feet flat on the floor and place your hands on your heart.","Visualize roots extending from your feet into the earth, connecting to your ancestors and land.","Inhale deeply, acknowledging the strength of those who came before you.","Exhale slowly, releasing the pressure of corporate expectations without judgment."],"reflection_questions":["How does my body feel when I acknowledge my roots?","What part of my identity feels most supportive right now?"],"journaling_prompt":"Describe the feeling of support you experience when connecting to your heritage during a stressful corporate situation.","closing_message":"You carry wisdom that predates this workplace. Trust it.","tags":["mindfulness","grounding","cultural-identity"]}
{"id":"indigenous-leader-burnout-003","category":"Burnout Recovery","subcategory":"Boundaries","content_type":"situation_based","title":"Setting Sustainable Boundaries","affirmation":"My boundaries protect my energy and respect my cultural commitments.","situation":"Being asked to take on additional corporate tasks while managing community obligations or cultural observances.","tone":"empowering","purpose":"Communicate capacity clearly without compromising cultural values or feeling guilt.","duration_minutes":null,"practice_steps":["Acknowledge the request to show it was heard, then pause before responding.","State current capacity: 'I am currently prioritizing community commitments that require my full attention.'","Propose a realistic alternative: 'I can address this task on Thursday morning.'","Remind yourself that protecting your time enables sustainable, long-term leadership."],"reflection_questions":["Do I feel a need to over-explain my cultural obligations?","How does setting this boundary serve my community long-term?"],"journaling_prompt":"Write about a recent request you wished you declined and draft a response for next time.","closing_message":"Clear boundaries are a form of self-respect. Your well-being is essential to your leadership effectiveness.","tags":["boundaries","communication","work-life-balance"]}
