{"id":"res-sea-26-001","category":"Resilience","subcategory":"Cultural Expectations","content_type":"practice","title":"Navigating Perfectionism with Cultural Grace","affirmation":"I honor my family's values while respecting my own limits and growth path.","situation":"Feeling overwhelmed by familial or societal pressure to achieve perfection in career and life.","tone":"grounding","purpose":"To build resilience against perfectionism using CBT and culturally sensitive reframes while asserting boundaries.","duration_minutes":20,"practice_steps":["Identify a specific expectation causing you stress today.","Acknowledge the love or intention behind the request.","Ask yourself: Is this expectation fact or a fear-based assumption?","Reframe duty as mutual care rather than strict compliance.","Communicate one small boundary respectfully using 'I' statements."],"reflection_questions":["What does success look like to me versus my family?","Where do our values align, and where do they differ?","How does prioritizing my well-being alongside my family's wishes feel?"],"journaling_prompt":"Write a letter to your family acknowledging their sacrifices and the values you cherish, then gently express where you need space to grow differently.","closing_message":"Progress is gradual; honoring yourself is part of honoring them.","tags":["CBT","boundaries","Southeast Asia","perfectionism","family dynamics"]}
{"id":"res-sea-26-002","category":"Resilience","subcategory":"Self-Worth","content_type":"affirmation","title":"Value Beyond Achievement","affirmation":"My value as a person is not defined by my productivity or meeting every expectation.","situation":null,"tone":"grounding","purpose":"Decouple self-worth from perfectionism","duration_minutes":2,"practice_steps":[],"reflection_questions":[],"journaling_prompt":"What are three things I value about myself that have nothing to do with my career or academic success?","closing_message":"You are enough exactly as you are today.","tags":["self-worth","perfectionism","mindset"]}
{"id":"res-sea-26-003","category":"Resilience","subcategory":"Cognitive Reframing","content_type":"situation_based","title":"Navigating a Mistake","affirmation":"Mistakes are a natural part of growth and do not erase my competence.","situation":"Making a visible error at work while feeling the weight of family expectations.","tone":"empowering","purpose":"Use CBT to challenge the all-or-nothing thinking associated with perfectionism.","duration_minutes":10,"practice_steps":["Pause and notice the physical sensation of the mistake.","Identify the automatic thought, such as 'I have failed everyone'.","Challenge the thought with evidence: 'Have I succeeded before? Is this mistake fatal?'","Create a balanced thought: 'I made a mistake, and I have the skills to fix it.'"],"reflection_questions":["What would I say to a friend in this exact situation?","Does this mistake truly define my entire career path?"],"journaling_prompt":"Describe a time a mistake actually led to a learning opportunity or a better outcome.","closing_message":"Growth happens in the space between the mistake and the recovery.","tags":["CBT","perfectionism","work-life"]}

