{"id": "boundary-001", "category": "Interpersonal Skills", "subcategory": "Boundaries", "content_type": "situation_based", "title": "Setting Boundaries with Close Friends", "affirmation": "My needs are valid, and true friends will respect my need for rest.", "situation": "Feeling guilty about declining an invitation from a best friend while experiencing burnout.", "tone": "gentle", "purpose": "To reduce guilt and communicate a need for rest without sacrificing the relationship.", "duration_minutes": 10, "practice_steps": ["Acknowledge the guilt but recognize the physical need for rest.", "Draft a message that validates the friendship while stating the boundary, such as: 'I care about you, but I'm overwhelmed and need to rest tonight.'", "Send the message and practice self-compassion while waiting for a response."], "reflection_questions": ["Why do I feel that saying no is a betrayal of the friendship?", "How does my body feel when I prioritize my rest?"], "journaling_prompt": "Describe a time when a friend respected your boundaries and how that strengthened the bond.", "closing_message": "Taking care of yourself allows you to show up more fully for others later.", "tags": ["burnout", "friendship", "guilt", "self-care"]}
{"id": "boundary-002", "category": "Interpersonal Skills", "subcategory": "Boundaries", "content_type": "situation_based", "title": "Setting Boundaries with Casual Acquaintances", "affirmation": "I can be polite and kind while still prioritizing my own mental energy.", "situation": "Declining a social outing with a casual acquaintance when energy levels are low.", "tone": "grounding", "purpose": "To maintain a polite distance while preserving energy.", "duration_minutes": 5, "practice_steps": ["Remind yourself that you are not responsible for another person's disappointment.", "Use a brief, clear statement of unavailability without over-explaining, such as: 'I appreciate the invite, but I won't be able to make it this time.'", "Focus on your breathing to ground yourself after the interaction."], "reflection_questions": ["Do I feel the need to over-explain my reasons for saying no?", "What is the worst-case scenario if this person is slightly disappointed?"], "journaling_prompt": "List three short phrases you can use to say no politely and firmly.", "closing_message": "Your energy is a limited resource; it is okay to spend it wisely.", "tags": ["social-energy", "boundaries", "acquaintances"]}
{"id": "boundary-003", "category": "Interpersonal Skills", "subcategory": "Boundaries", "content_type": "situation_based", "title": "Setting Boundaries in Group Dynamics", "affirmation": "I am allowed to step back from group activities to recover my strength.", "situation": "Feeling pressured by a group of peers to attend an event during a period of burnout.", "tone": "empowering", "purpose": "To resist peer pressure and honor personal limits.", "duration_minutes": 15, "practice_steps": ["Identify the specific feeling of pressure, such as FOMO or guilt.", "Practice a script: 'I'm taking a step back to recharge. Hope you all have a great time.'", "Visualize yourself feeling relieved after choosing rest over pressure."], "reflection_questions": ["How does the fear of missing out conflict with my need for recovery?", "Who in the group is most likely to be supportive of my decision?"], "journaling_prompt": "Write about the difference between 'missing out' and 'missing a chance to recover'.", "closing_message": "Protecting your energy is an act of care, not rejection.", "tags": ["peer-pressure", "burnout", "group-dynamics", "self-care"]}

{"id": "soc-conf-routine-01", "category": "Social Confidence", "subcategory": "Language Learning", "content_type": "practice", "title": "Cross-Cultural Social Confidence Routine", "affirmation": "Making mistakes while learning a language is normal and does not define my worth.", "situation": "Navigating social interactions where a language barrier triggers social anxiety.", "tone": "realistic", "purpose": "To build confidence through exposure and cognitive reframing of social missteps.", "duration_minutes": 15, "practice_steps": ["Recite the affirmation before leaving home to ground yourself.", "Identify one low-stakes social interaction for the day.", "Pause and take three deep breaths before entering the social space.", "If you stumble on a word, smile and try again, or ask for clarification.", "Afterward, note one thing you communicated successfully, regardless of grammar."], "reflection_questions": ["What evidence do I have that people judged me harshly?", "How would I treat a friend who made the same mistakes?"], "journaling_prompt": "Describe a recent social mistake. Write down three alternative explanations for what happened that do not involve personal inadequacy.", "closing_message": "You are building a bridge between cultures, and that takes time and bravery.", "tags": ["cbt", "social-anxiety", "immigrant-experience", "language-barrier", "cognitive-reframing"]}
