{"id":"social-media-reframe-001","category":"Digital Wellness","subcategory":"Social Comparison","content_type":"situation_based","title":"The Curation Reality Check","affirmation":"I am comparing my unfiltered reality to someone else's carefully curated and edited highlight reel.","situation":"Scrolling through social media and feeling anxious about not meeting an idealized standard.","tone":"realistic","purpose":"To challenge the authenticity of online personas.","duration_minutes":5,"practice_steps":["Pause scrolling and put the phone down for a few minutes.","Acknowledge the feeling of comparison arising without judgment.","Remind yourself that lighting, angles, and filters are tools that shape what you see, not reality.","Ask yourself if you are comparing your behind-the-scenes to their highlight reel."],"reflection_questions":["What emotions arise when I view this image?","What parts of this persona are likely edited, staged, or incomplete?"],"journaling_prompt":"List three things about your day that are real and meaningful, regardless of how they would look in a photo.","closing_message":"Your reality is valid, even if it isn't posted.","tags":["social-media","comparison","digital-wellness"]}
{"id":"mirror-work-routine-001","category":"Self-Acceptance","subcategory":"Body Neutrality","content_type":"practice","title":"Neutral Observation Routine","affirmation":"My body allows me to experience life, and that function is enough.","situation":"Daily routine to shift from critical judgment to neutral observation.","tone":"gentle","purpose":"To foster neutral-to-positive body neutrality over time.","duration_minutes":15,"practice_steps":["Stand in front of a mirror for two minutes, breathing deeply and placing a hand over your heart.","Look at a part of your body without judgment, describing it using factual, non-judgmental language.","Acknowledge the function of that body part rather than focusing on form.","Name three non-appearance traits you appreciate about yourself.","Write down one thing your body allowed you to do today."],"reflection_questions":["Can I observe my body without assigning a value of 'good' or 'bad'?","What did it feel like to look in the mirror without judging?"],"journaling_prompt":"Describe your body's strengths in terms of what it enables you to do, rather than how it looks.","closing_message":"Progress is non-linear; be patient with yourself as you navigate this shift in perspective.","tags":["mirror-work","body-neutrality","mindfulness","journaling"]}

